# Read by BuildKit when building with `-f infra/docker/Dockerfile` (takes precedence over a root
# .dockerignore). Keep the build context to what the Dockerfile COPYs.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src/
!contracts/
!data/regions/
# The committed runtime inputs the service reads through RUPTURE_REPO_ROOT (see the Dockerfile:
# the risk scenario/exposure/GSIM/vulnerability tables and the two aftershock sequence slices).
# Re-including a nested path needs each parent walked back in, hence the ladder: `!tests` then
# `tests/*` then the two directories that are wanted. The rest of tests/ stays out of the context.
!tests
tests/*
!tests/fixtures
tests/fixtures/*
!tests/fixtures/risk/
!tests/fixtures/aftershock/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
